#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203857 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204079 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c676a83b-f3d4-579b-ab54-de2104552e8f" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Gradient of a Function With Respect to a Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "ca1002c8-c615-5f7b-8876-82cf87c8864f" :question/math-academy-id "e-17349" :question/problem "Consider the function $f: \\mathbb{R}^{2 \\times 2} \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}$ defined by \n\n$$\nf(X) = (\\det(X))^2.\n$$\n\n \n\nWhat is the gradient of $f$ with respect to $X$ at ![](images/70/70a078e9f26d91a1beb588e88c812057b85d31586576c94eaa510dedba7da2f0.svg)" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of a function $f: \\mathbb{R}^{m \\times n} \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}$ with respect to a matrix $X \\in \\mathbb{R}^{m \\times n}$ is\n![](images/26/26b51d20ec90168f9bf7602ed9e5f05cb4a5fb1421bb52fd0042ff81faa5f8ab.svg)\n\nIn our case, writing out the function $f(X)$ where ![](images/db/dbd3e061ec5b3c6e148c347b0bf829391218f883ba4e6b1271bf8f65fb08d38b.svg), we get\n\n$$\nf(X) = (\\det(X))^2 = (x_{11}x_{22} - x_{12}x_{21})^2.\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,{∇}_{X}f(X) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{11}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{12}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{21}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{22}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{11}}({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})^{2} & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{12}}({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})^{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{21}}({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})^{2} & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{22}}({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})^{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})\\cdot {x}_{22} & 2({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})\\cdot (-{x}_{21}) \\\\ 2({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})\\cdot (-{x}_{12}) & 2({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})\\cdot {x}_{11}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =2({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{22} & -{x}_{21} \\\\ -{x}_{12} & {x}_{11}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =2det(X)[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{22} & -{x}_{21} \\\\ -{x}_{12} & {x}_{11}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ![](images/79/790980ee64747a4ef3becd801431083d66839972cb271207807c43c53cf166fa.svg) we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{X}f(X) & =2(-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 10-(-4)\\cdot \\frac{3}{2})[\\begin{aligned}10 & 4 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =2(-5-(-6))[\\begin{aligned}10 & 4 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}20 & 8 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203866 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204081 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef7b2139-06eb-5584-a267-d9fbc9b5d041" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Chain Rule to Calculate Gradients"}] :question/id #uuid "429a6a34-2fe5-5c09-9b74-e4b650209007" :question/math-academy-id "e-17870" :question/problem "Consider the function $L: \\mathbb{R}^{2 \\times 3}   \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}$ defined by $L(\\mathbf{A}) = \\dfrac{1}{2}(\\mathbf{A}\\mathbf{x} - \\mathbf{b})^T(\\mathbf{A}\\mathbf{x} - \\mathbf{b}),$ where\n![](images/51/518bfea30c779d3e9dc1ab6b77b0ddaa9b938b56b0bb3b9e68d6c9b9cdae5666.svg)\nWhat is $\\nabla_{\\mathbf{A}} L$ at \n![](images/a1/a1e2b39a295cebfd8425e8ab73e4d915233ca3afbd4141c54332c38f1091be15.svg)" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of $L$ with respect to $\\mathbf{A}$ is a matrix of the same shape as $\\mathbf{A}$, with $(i,j)$th entry given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial L}{\\partial a_{ij}},\n$$\n\nthe partial derivative of $L$ with respect to the $(i,j)$th entry of $\\mathbf{A}.$\n\nWe can compute $\\dfrac{\\partial L}{\\partial a_{ij}}$ by applying the chain rule.\n\nLet $\\mathbf{y} = \\mathbf{A}\\mathbf{x} - \\mathbf{b} \\in \\mathbb{R}^2.$ Then, $L(\\mathbf{A}) = \\dfrac{1}{2}\\mathbf{y}^T\\mathbf{y}$ and\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial L}{\\partial a_{ij}} = \\sum_{k=1}^2 \\dfrac{\\partial L}{\\partial y_k} \\cdot \\dfrac{\\partial y_k}{\\partial a_{ij}}\n$$\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n\\nabla_{\\mathbf{y}} L = \\nabla_{\\mathbf{y}} \\bigg( \\dfrac{1}{2}\\mathbf{y}^T\\mathbf{y} \\bigg) = \\mathbf{y},\n$$\n\nwe have that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial L}{\\partial y_k} = y_k.\n$$\n\nWriting out $\\mathbf{y} = \\mathbf{A}\\mathbf{x} - \\mathbf{b}$ in component-wise notation as \n\n$$\ny_i = \\sum\\limits_{j=1}^3 (a_{ij} x_j - b_i),\n$$\n\nwe have \n\n- $\\dfrac{\\partial y_k}{\\partial a_{ij}} = x_j$ if $i = k$, and\n\n- $\\dfrac{\\partial y_k}{\\partial a_{ij}} = 0$ if $i \\neq k.$\n\nThis means that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}} & ={\\sum }_{k=1}^{2}\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{i}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{i}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & ={y}_{i}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{i}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & ={y}_{i}{x}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $(i,j)$th entry of $\\nabla_{\\mathbf{A}} L$ is the $i$th entry of $\\mathbf{y}$ multiplied by the $j$th entry of $\\mathbf{x}$, so\n\n$$\n\\nabla_{\\mathbf{A}} L = \\mathbf{y} \\cdot \\mathbf{x}^T.\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating $\\nabla_{\\mathbf{A}} L$ at ![](images/ee/ee9b9f891c92caf4229e8e92c20031fe7ba9e1cc0472105caf5a6cfaa8541a27.svg) we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{A}L & =y\\cdot {x}^{T} \\\\  & =(Ax-b)\\cdot {x}^{T} \\\\  & =([\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}])\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =([\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}])\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203871 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204080 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "35dc17b6-1c82-55ec-9657-20f2850794e5" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Gradient of a Function Component-Wise"}] :question/id #uuid "5aa67862-6f7a-57ac-9473-d039fc4bfec4" :question/math-academy-id "e-17951" :question/problem "Consider the function $L: \\mathbb{R}^{2 \\times 3} \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}$ defined by $L(\\mathbf{A}) = \\mathbf{y}^T\\mathbf{A}\\mathbf{x}$ where \n![](images/1d/1ddd8273660c1a84671e442af51d78ecc3df160fc0b807695c12297300118aa8.svg)\nWhat is $\\nabla_{\\mathbf{A}} L$ at \n![](images/c6/c66b8dc8fde116a844d833de35034c534b650a9b7f788eef8366e770f6923380.svg)" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of $L$ with respect to $\\mathbf{A}$ is a matrix of the same shape as $\\mathbf{A}$, with $(i,j)$th entry given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial L}{\\partial a_{ij}},\n$$\n\nthe partial derivative of $L$ with respect to the $(i,j)$th entry of $\\mathbf{A}.$\n\nWriting out $L$ in component-wise notation as \n\n$$\nL = \\sum\\limits_{i=1}^2 \\sum\\limits_{j=1}^3 a_{ij} y_i x_j,\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial L}{\\partial a_{ij}} = y_i x_j.\n$$\n\nThus, $\\nabla_{\\mathbf{A}} L = \\mathbf{y} \\cdot \\mathbf{x}^T.$\n\nEvaluating at the given values ![](images/d8/d8a406621f1e60112d233f79cdde2e1405681554510ac4ea6af68409b4af4676.svg) and ![](images/df/dfa340dc46ddf622d0a16fdf8335a5183786294d395201e48f9adee4182bd91d.svg) we get\n\n![](images/b6/b6250171f2d99fb806cbb449b18f3a9c0513d8eac898d256d020e0b2cb986f8b.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204564 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204079 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c676a83b-f3d4-579b-ab54-de2104552e8f" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Gradient of a Function With Respect to a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c47d4b1-a923-5d13-9ea2-f25e49d50c60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203338} {:answer/id #uuid "23f517c8-02d6-5cbc-bbf1-171ed91219de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533229} {:answer/id #uuid "3edc160a-8101-5d90-8138-2690348d912d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533286} {:answer/id #uuid "dd2c45f0-ab57-5f4c-af72-1b497341005f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533683} {:answer/id #uuid "efa876a3-a667-54e0-abff-4b40c1125d55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533727}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd2c45f0-ab57-5f4c-af72-1b497341005f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533683} :answer-field/id #uuid "18959201-dc75-5139-b452-5ab59d2a87d2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203333}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8781dff9-d5f6-57b2-92f1-799f898568b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-264512" :question/problem "Consider the function $f:{R}^{2\\times 2}\\to R$ defined by \n\n$$\nf(X)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(det(X)).\n$$\n\n \nWhat is the gradient of $f$ with respect to $X$ at $X=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of a function $f:{R}^{m\\times n}\\to R$ with respect to a matrix $X\\in {R}^{m\\times n}$ is\n\n$$\n{∇}_{X}f(X)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{11}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{12}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{1n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{21}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{22}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{2n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{m1}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{m2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{mn}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, writing out the function $f(X)$ where $X=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{11} & {x}_{12} \\\\ {x}_{21} & {x}_{22}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{2\\times 2}$, we get\n\n$$\nf(X)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(det(X))=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21}).\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,{∇}_{X}f(X) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{11}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{12}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{21}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{22}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{11}}(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{12}}(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{21}}(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{22}}(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21}))\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-{x}_{22}}{{x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21}} & \\frac{{x}_{21}}{{x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21}} \\\\ \\frac{{x}_{12}}{{x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21}} & \\frac{-{x}_{11}}{{x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21}}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $X=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n{∇}_{X}f(X)=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{4-1} & \\frac{1}{4-1} \\\\ \\frac{1}{4-1} & -\\frac{2}{4-1}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533993 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204079 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c676a83b-f3d4-579b-ab54-de2104552e8f" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Gradient of a Function With Respect to a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "395065b4-ace6-5290-9bf5-9ae34338d260" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533272} {:answer/id #uuid "a7154eb4-bcc0-5f39-b2ae-a197b10dfcda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533543} {:answer/id #uuid "d1260309-ef28-5201-b8ae-5cf3e6edba2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533649} {:answer/id #uuid "d548f9e6-0754-56f7-b875-8b2dee34bc68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533659} {:answer/id #uuid "e8c5a65a-fc58-5834-95f8-09e9880a2408" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533712}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1260309-ef28-5201-b8ae-5cf3e6edba2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533649} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c4e1c8c-757e-5673-8cd0-b270c0c3c7e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533898}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "378ecb1a-5423-57cf-9a92-70fe30005016" :question/math-academy-id "q-265773" :question/problem "Consider the function $f:{R}^{2\\times 2}\\to R$ defined by \n\n$$\nf(X)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(det(X)).\n$$\n\n \nWhat is the gradient of $f$ with respect to $X$ at $X=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of a function $f:{R}^{m\\times n}\\to R$ with respect to a matrix $X\\in {R}^{m\\times n}$ is\n\n$$\n{∇}_{X}f(X)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{11}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{12}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{1n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{21}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{22}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{2n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{m1}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{m2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{mn}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, writing out the function $f(X)$ where $X=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{11} & {x}_{12} \\\\ {x}_{21} & {x}_{22}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{2\\times 2}$, we get\n\n$$\nf(X)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(det(X))=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21}).\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,{∇}_{X}f(X) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{11}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{12}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{21}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{22}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{11}}(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{12}}(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{21}}(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{22}}(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21}))\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-{x}_{22}}{{x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21}} & \\frac{{x}_{21}}{{x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21}} \\\\ \\frac{{x}_{12}}{{x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21}} & \\frac{-{x}_{11}}{{x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21}}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $X=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n{∇}_{X}f(X)=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{-4-(-3)} & \\frac{1}{-4-(-3)} \\\\ \\frac{-3}{-4-(-3)} & -\\frac{(-1)}{-4-(-3)}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{-1} & \\frac{1}{-1} \\\\ \\frac{-3}{-1} & -\\frac{(-1)}{-1}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204572 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204079 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c676a83b-f3d4-579b-ab54-de2104552e8f" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Gradient of a Function With Respect to a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ea4ca45-df67-56c6-911d-3d71844ae6f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533285} {:answer/id #uuid "4fe9b706-ba42-57d7-b61f-d9a640eeeedb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 & 16 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533333} {:answer/id #uuid "650ab510-72e3-535b-b721-0beb1e22eb23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 8 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533374} {:answer/id #uuid "c0d59bb6-b177-593a-b402-558045a82d46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 2 \\\\ 8 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533605} {:answer/id #uuid "fabfae26-7434-5570-8009-28ae299dc640" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 & -8 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533753}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "650ab510-72e3-535b-b721-0beb1e22eb23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 8 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533374} :answer-field/id #uuid "006b5aba-a8d4-5887-b052-f91f00560b87" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203370}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "52069b73-e5e5-5970-bfc8-fea272282f4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-265775" :question/problem "Consider the function $f:{R}^{2\\times 2}\\to R$ defined by \n\n$$\nf(X)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}{x}_{ij}^{2}\n$$\n\n \nwhere ${x}_{ij}$ are the corresponding matrix's entries. What is the gradient of $f$ with respect to $X$ at $X=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of a function $f:{R}^{m\\times n}\\to R$ with respect to a matrix $X\\in {R}^{m\\times n}$ is\n\n$$\n{∇}_{X}f(X)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{11}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{12}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{1n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{21}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{22}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{2n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{m1}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{m2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{mn}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, writing out the function $f(X)$ where $X=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{11} & {x}_{12} \\\\ {x}_{21} & {x}_{22}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{2\\times 2}$, we get\n\n$$\nf(X)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}{x}_{ij}^{2}=({x}_{11}^{2}+{x}_{12}^{2}+{x}_{21}^{2}+{x}_{22}^{2}).\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,{∇}_{X}f(X) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{11}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{12}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{21}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{22}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{11}}({x}_{11}^{2}+{x}_{12}^{2}+{x}_{21}^{2}+{x}_{22}^{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{12}}({x}_{11}^{2}+{x}_{12}^{2}+{x}_{21}^{2}+{x}_{22}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{21}}({x}_{11}^{2}+{x}_{12}^{2}+{x}_{21}^{2}+{x}_{22}^{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{22}}({x}_{11}^{2}+{x}_{12}^{2}+{x}_{21}^{2}+{x}_{22}^{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{11} & 2{x}_{12} \\\\ 2{x}_{21} & 2{x}_{22}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{11} & {x}_{12} \\\\ {x}_{21} & {x}_{22}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =2X.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $X=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n{∇}_{X}f(X)=[\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot (-3) & 2\\cdot (4) \\\\ 2\\cdot (1) & 2\\cdot (-2)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 8 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533992 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204079 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c676a83b-f3d4-579b-ab54-de2104552e8f" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Gradient of a Function With Respect to a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65feaefc-9540-5e9e-aba0-1a7effe2a8bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}56 & -14 \\\\ 42 & 14\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533378} {:answer/id #uuid "87069efe-45b4-5333-8a10-7ed32590e859" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533459} {:answer/id #uuid "90d505d3-8405-52e7-b05e-824d062628e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}14 & 42 \\\\ -14 & 56\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533488} {:answer/id #uuid "d975b5e6-4b40-557d-ac26-27b4762c7188" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}14 & -42 \\\\ 14 & 56\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533671} {:answer/id #uuid "fe0899b4-0eb5-5f96-802e-1c29cc2efdb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 21 \\\\ -7 & 28\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533763}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d975b5e6-4b40-557d-ac26-27b4762c7188" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}14 & -42 \\\\ 14 & 56\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533671} :answer-field/id #uuid "51ec136b-c0f0-5734-828b-fc93c68cab5a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533846}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "35662c2c-d0a2-5e1c-b319-cae7bd255ca0" :question/math-academy-id "q-265777" :question/problem "Consider the function $f:{R}^{2\\times 2}\\to R$ defined by \n\n$$\nf(X)=(det(X))^{2}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWhat is the gradient of $f$ with respect to $X$ at $X=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of a function $f:{R}^{m\\times n}\\to R$ with respect to a matrix $X\\in {R}^{m\\times n}$ is\n\n$$\n{∇}_{X}f(X)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{11}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{12}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{1n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{21}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{22}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{2n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{m1}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{m2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{mn}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, writing out the function $f(X)$ where $X=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{11} & {x}_{12} \\\\ {x}_{21} & {x}_{22}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{2\\times 2}$, we get\n\n$$\nf(X)=(det(X))^{2}=({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})^{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,{∇}_{X}f(X) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{11}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{12}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{21}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{22}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{11}}({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})^{2} & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{12}}({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})^{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{21}}({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})^{2} & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{22}}({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})^{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})\\cdot {x}_{22} & 2({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})\\cdot (-{x}_{21}) \\\\ 2({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})\\cdot (-{x}_{12}) & 2({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})\\cdot {x}_{11}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =2({x}_{11}{x}_{22}-{x}_{12}{x}_{21})[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{22} & -{x}_{21} \\\\ -{x}_{12} & {x}_{11}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =2det(X)[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{22} & -{x}_{21} \\\\ -{x}_{12} & {x}_{11}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $X=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n{∇}_{X}f(X)=2(4\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 3)[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}14 & -42 \\\\ 14 & 56\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534003 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204079 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c676a83b-f3d4-579b-ab54-de2104552e8f" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Gradient of a Function With Respect to a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e4db12b-c1a2-5b3a-90cc-1eec8b8e9e29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 10 \\\\ 6 & 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533211} {:answer/id #uuid "361becea-d4d4-5a84-ac95-a90decebb407" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533266} {:answer/id #uuid "881b05f3-5a11-54ed-9622-0e746ae1581b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 10 \\\\ -6 & 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533464} {:answer/id #uuid "8dd57312-bdfb-5065-a149-96de4be679e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 15 \\\\ -9 & 12\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533482} {:answer/id #uuid "d21d4e11-51b9-5d89-985a-ece3e742b405" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -10 \\\\ -6 & 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533651}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "881b05f3-5a11-54ed-9622-0e746ae1581b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 10 \\\\ -6 & 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533464} :answer-field/id #uuid "479c37e2-c9fe-54cc-8640-7226558adb45" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533838}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4c895033-c45a-5568-ba41-7003b1ce0b16" :question/math-academy-id "q-265980" :question/problem "Consider the function $f:{R}^{2\\times 2}\\to R$ defined by \n\n$$\nf(X)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}{x}_{ij}^{2}\n$$\n\n \nwhere ${x}_{ij}$ are the corresponding matrix's entries. What is the gradient of $f$ with respect to $X$ at $X=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of a function $f:{R}^{m\\times n}\\to R$ with respect to a matrix $X\\in {R}^{m\\times n}$ is\n\n$$\n{∇}_{X}f(X)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{11}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{12}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{1n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{21}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{22}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{2n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{m1}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{m2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{mn}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, writing out the function $f(X)$ where $X=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{11} & {x}_{12} \\\\ {x}_{21} & {x}_{22}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{2\\times 2}$, we get\n\n$$\nf(X)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}{x}_{ij}^{2}=({x}_{11}^{2}+{x}_{12}^{2}+{x}_{21}^{2}+{x}_{22}^{2}).\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,{∇}_{X}f(X) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{11}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{12}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{21}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{22}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{11}}({x}_{11}^{2}+{x}_{12}^{2}+{x}_{21}^{2}+{x}_{22}^{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{12}}({x}_{11}^{2}+{x}_{12}^{2}+{x}_{21}^{2}+{x}_{22}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{21}}({x}_{11}^{2}+{x}_{12}^{2}+{x}_{21}^{2}+{x}_{22}^{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{22}}({x}_{11}^{2}+{x}_{12}^{2}+{x}_{21}^{2}+{x}_{22}^{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{11} & 2{x}_{12} \\\\ 2{x}_{21} & 2{x}_{22}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{11} & {x}_{12} \\\\ {x}_{21} & {x}_{22}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =2X.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $X=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n{∇}_{X}f(X)=[\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot (1) & 2\\cdot (5) \\\\ 2\\cdot (-3) & 2\\cdot (4)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 10 \\\\ -6 & 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534008 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204080 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "35dc17b6-1c82-55ec-9657-20f2850794e5" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Gradient of a Function Component-Wise"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0dad9073-478b-54b1-a7af-14e9b549d134" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 6 \\\\ 14 & 10 \\\\ -15 & -35\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533174} {:answer/id #uuid "0f783940-c57e-5b76-b2a2-204a0ec5ec07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 6 & 14 \\\\ 10 & -15 & -35\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533178} {:answer/id #uuid "9d1db3e7-b40d-5dd2-8056-ba5fbb14c5dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}12 & 30 \\\\ 18 & 45 \\\\ 42 & 105\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533520} {:answer/id #uuid "a46cedc9-7f50-57d8-8219-01fc7f258e44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533537} {:answer/id #uuid "cdb01e9d-e482-500b-8961-81b00c565787" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-12 & 18 & 42 \\\\ 30 & -45 & -105\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533637}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cdb01e9d-e482-500b-8961-81b00c565787" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-12 & 18 & 42 \\\\ 30 & -45 & -105\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533637} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6ef3817-fd8a-50ea-a054-edd21587414d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533962}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "55449077-495e-5404-a705-ef8294705226" :question/math-academy-id "q-269371" :question/problem "Consider the function $L:{R}^{2\\times 3}\\to R$ defined by $L(A)=3({y}^{T}Ax)$ where \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{A}L$ at \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of $L$ with respect to $A$ is a matrix of the same shape as $A$, with $(i,j)$th entry given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}},\n$$\n\nthe partial derivative of $L$ with respect to the $(i,j)$th entry of $A.$\n\nWriting out $L$ in component-wise notation as \n\n$$\nL={\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}3{a}_{ij}{y}_{i}{x}_{j},\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}=3{y}_{i}{x}_{j}.\n$$\n\nThus, ${∇}_{A}L=3(y\\cdot {x}^{T}).$\n\nEvaluating at the given values $x=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n{∇}_{A}L=3([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & 7\\end{aligned}])=3([\\begin{aligned}-4 & 6 & 14 \\\\ 10 & -15 & -35\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}-12 & 18 & 42 \\\\ 30 & -45 & -105\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534000 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204080 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "35dc17b6-1c82-55ec-9657-20f2850794e5" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Gradient of a Function Component-Wise"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answ