in{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of $L$ with respect to $A$ is a matrix of the same shape as $A$, with $(i,j)$th entry given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}},\n$$\n\nthe partial derivative of $L$ with respect to the $(i,j)$th entry of $A.$\n\nWriting out $L$ in component-wise notation as \n\n$$\nL={\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}{a}_{ij}{y}_{i}{x}_{j},\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}={y}_{i}{x}_{j}.\n$$\n\nThus, ${∇}_{A}L=y\\cdot {x}^{T}.$\n\nEvaluating at the given values $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n{∇}_{A}L=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534029 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204080 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "35dc17b6-1c82-55ec-9657-20f2850794e5" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Gradient of a Function Component-Wise"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56eeb979-bf72-5af2-b0de-d329747584af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-40 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533343} {:answer/id #uuid "7af10c05-dd89-5b9c-85e8-ac267c31a704" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-30 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533431} {:answer/id #uuid "86291e0b-5df9-5de7-8b90-d677970284b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-40 & 8 \\\\ 10 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533456} {:answer/id #uuid "d8c303b2-7786-51c5-872c-00f11a1d607b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-40 & 10 \\\\ 8 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533670} {